From b5a4828c2156cd2b0d13679ed2fec9e27dea041b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 23:29:01 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui+agent): Stop ends exactly the holder's automated
 turn; bounded retiring retries

Round-2 review of #3908:
- Stop no longer blocks the RPC reader: only cheap checks run inline (no local turn,
  automated newest turn, ledger state); holder discovery and the end run on a worker
  and report by error events.
- Targeted end instead of the registry take-over: automated turns stamp their kind in
  the durable lease holder (``:auto=<kind>``, agent/turn_facade_lease.lease_holder);
  SessionDB.request_turn_end records an end request only while that exact holder holds
  the lease (compare-and-set into session_turn_end_requests); the holding process's
  DurableTurnLease tick honours it with the agent's ordinary interrupt (no lease loss),
  so the lease is released as usual and a queued forwarded admission runs once. Used
  whether or not a prompt is queued. A gateway without turn-end-request-v1 keeps the
  take-over only when its ledger is empty; with a prompt queued the chat is told the
  message runs when the background turn ends. Gateway FIFO notice turns carry the same
  holder stamp, so the request is fenced to that exact turn generation.
- _retiring_busy records (retry_at, written_at); a record older than 30 s is ignored.
- Retiring-owner short retries stop after 10 per notice row; then ordinary busy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
